---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About the SympleHost Knowledge Base"
  description="What the SympleHost Knowledge Base is, who it is for, and how it relates to the SympleHost product."
>
  <article class="prose-page">
    <h1>About the SympleHost Knowledge Base</h1>
    <p>
      This site is the official help center for <strong>SympleHost</strong>, an AI co-host and
      property management platform for short-term rentals. It publishes setup guides, feature
      explanations, FAQs, webinars, and walkthroughs so hosts and operators can configure messaging,
      channels, pricing, operations, and direct bookings without waiting on a support ticket.
    </p>
    <p>
      Content is maintained for hosts running one listing and for operators managing larger portfolios
      across Airbnb, Booking.com, Vrbo, Agoda, Expedia, Trip.com, and direct booking sites. Articles
      are written in plain language, kept in sync with the product, and available in English with
      localized paths for Japanese and Indonesian where translations exist.
    </p>
    <h2>Who this site is for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Hosts setting up SympleHost for the first time</li>
      <li>Operations managers automating turnovers, tasks, and guest messaging</li>
      <li>Partners and integrators reading the Partner API surface</li>
      <li>AI agents retrieving documentation via HTML, markdown endpoints, or llms.txt</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How this relates to the product</h2>
    <p>
      The knowledge base explains how SympleHost works. Live account data — reservations, inbox
      threads, pricing rules, and tasks — lives in the SympleHost application and, where enabled, the
      SympleHost MCP connector for AI assistants. Use this site for procedures and concepts; use the
      product or MCP for account-specific state.
    </p>
    <p>
      Product website: <a href="https://www.symplehost.ai">https://www.symplehost.ai</a><br />
      Support: <a href="mailto:support@symplehost.ai">support@symplehost.ai</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose-page { max-width: 42rem; margin: 0 auto; }
  .prose-page h1 { font-size: 1.75rem; color: var(--heading-color); margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .prose-page h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--heading-color); margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem; }
  .prose-page p, .prose-page li { color: var(--foreground); line-height: 1.65; margin-bottom: 0.85rem; }
  .prose-page ul { margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem 1.25rem; }
  .prose-page a { color: var(--primary); }
</style>
